  "question": "If $A$ and $B$ are $2\\times2$ symmetric matrices, which of the following is true for $AB-BA$?",
  "answeroption": "B",
  "explanation": "Let $A$ and $B$ be symmetric: $A^T = A$, $B^T = B$.<br /><br />$(AB-BA)^T = B^T A^T - A^T B^T = BA - AB = - (AB - BA)$.<br /><br />So $AB-BA$ is skew symmetric.",
  "explanation_image": [],
  "options": {
    "A": "$AB - BA$ is a symmetric matrix",
    "B": "$AB - BA$ is a skew-symmetric matrix",
    "C": "$AB - BA$ is a zero matrix",
    "D": "$AB - BA$ is an identity matrix"
  },
